      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the observed historical correlation is compelling, relying too heavily on ethnicity or demographic composition as a sole predictor can introduce bias and raise ethical concerns for underwriting purposes. Predictive models should strive for identifying functional risk drivers, not targeting protected characteristics. Instead of heavily weighting raw ethnic composition, consider transforming these variables into metrics that measure socioeconomic stress or changes in neighborhood stability, which may be more actionable for risk assessment.",
